  "assumptions": [
    "Synthetic external magnetic flux-density response from uniformly magnetized prisms only; no reference-field correction, inversion, uncertainty or unique geological interpretation.",
    "All bounds/points/background/magnetisation share an explicit local Cartesian metre/x_y_up frame and height datum. No north/datum/CRS conversion or induced-only direction is inferred.",
    "Magnetisation components are A/m; bounds_m order xmin,xmax,ymin,ymax,zmin,zmax. No susceptibility, demagnetisation or finite-body interior magnetics is inferred.",
    "Every point must lie outside every closed prism by at least explicit min_distance_m, including zero magnetisation sources. Interiors/faces/edges/corners are excluded atomically.",
    "The existing aspect/point-offset conditioning domain and lower-corner local origins apply. No silent dipole approximation or softening.",
    "Harmonica returns nT with up-directed components. Choclo0.3.2 permeability is explicitly rescaled to CODATA2022 to align native dipoles; both constants/versions are checked.",
    "Linear and exact TMI use SUMMED vector and fixed explicit background; exact magnitude difference is nonlinear and not additive. Without background, all TMI outputs are null.",
    "Three per-source fixed-geometry magnetisation-component derivatives cover vectors and LINEAR TMI only in nT/(A/m); no exact-TMI/geometry derivatives or inversion.",
    "Python optional backend performs numerical execution. JavaScript/core Python validate portable requests without the optional extra.",
    "External-distance and background-magnitude guards compare fixed-order binary64 squared norms; equal computed squares are accepted. Distance diagnostics use sqrt of that same squared sum."
  ],
  "references": [
    "https://www.fatiando.org/harmonica/v0.7.0/api/generated/harmonica.prism_magnetic.html",
    "https://www.fatiando.org/choclo/v0.3.2/api/generated/choclo.prism.magnetic_field.html",
    "https://physics.nist.gov/cuu/Constants/Table/allascii.txt"
  ]
